# 18. GRAPH JSON FORMAT FOR FUTURE MERMAID FRONTEND

Do not generate Mermaid syntax in the backend.

Return structured graph JSON.

Example:

{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "type": "METHOD",
      "label": "OrderController.getOrders()",
      "classId": "c1",
      "moduleId": "mod1",
      "incomingCount": 0,
      "outgoingCount": 1,
      "relevanceScore": 0.75
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "type": "METHOD",
      "label": "OrderService.findOrders()",
      "classId": "c2",
      "moduleId": "mod1",
      "incomingCount": 5,
      "outgoingCount": 3,
      "relevanceScore": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "id": "e1",
      "source": "m1",
      "target": "m2",
      "type": "CALLS",
      "resolution": "EXACT"
    }
  ],
  "totalNodes": 2,
  "totalEdges": 1,
  "truncated": false
}

Support:

- Method-level graph
- Class-level graph
- Package-level graph
- Module-level graph
- Impact graph
- Dependency graph

The frontend will convert JSON into Mermaid diagrams.

Keep graph DTOs independent of visualization libraries.

